(text "Rack DIN rail: PSU, U201, K201, F201, terminal blocks for +24V / 0V. Spare station: S205–S207 and J202.\nInputs: switches connect +24V to Xn, S/S to 0V (sourcing). Outputs Y0–Y3 sink (NPN): lamps and K201 IN\ngo between +24V and Yn. UP = +24V, ZP = 0V power the PLC's transistor outputs.\nDock power: K201 closes only while Y0 = M0 AND X4 AND X5 AND watchdog OK (ladder, 03 §4). The E-stop's\nsecond NC contact feeds K201's DC+, so a pressed E-stop drops the relay in hardware.\nJ202 mates with the robot's charging pads (robot sheet J102): + on the right, − on the left, viewed from\nthe robot. 24 V reaches the pads only while the robot is docked and X4 is closed.\nThe rack's own dock has no switch and no contacts (01 §4): the robot's NOSE switch confirms docking there." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 223.52 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left top)) (uuid "fe1b42ba-349a-5064-942f-4a3fbdb0f145"))
(embedded_fonts no)
